{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game rule game rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","fileName":"Game Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Rule","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]] · [[Game Definition and Forms]] [[Play Design Elements]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Definition and Forms","Play Design Elements","Game Verb","Cognitive Load","Systemic Elegance","Player Mental Model","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game rule game rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","fileName":"Game Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Rule","heading":"Game Rule","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game rule specifies allowable behavior or a transition between states. Some rules are [[Game Verb|verbs]] that let the player act, while others determine how tokens behave, how resources change, and how objects respond.\n\nToo few rules can leave important situations ambiguous, while too many rules and exceptions restrict agency and increase [[Cognitive Load]]. Consistent rules support [[Systemic Elegance]] and help players build a reliable [[Player Mental Model]].\n\nThe experience of play comes from rules interacting rather than operating in isolation. Rules become more useful as the player discovers their relationships and applies them in increasingly developed situations.\n\nA complete ruleset may specify required, permitted, and prohibited actions; sequence of play; challenges and actions; goals; termination conditions; the meanings of symbols; and metarules that govern whether another rule may change. Software can hide bookkeeping rules from a video-game player while still enforcing them precisely.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Definition and Forms","Play Design Elements","Game Verb","Cognitive Load","Systemic Elegance","Player Mental Model","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game rule game rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Rule.md","fileName":"Game Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Rule","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]\n[[gamesdesignandplay.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Definition and Forms","Play Design Elements","Game Verb","Cognitive Load","Systemic Elegance","Player Mental Model","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}